here is guicorn with nginx


Got it. If you’re running **Gunicorn** behind **Nginx**, you can terminate HTTPS at Nginx using a **self-signed SSL certificate** and forward requests to Gunicorn over HTTP locally. This is very common for **internal or local production environments**. 🔐

I'll walk you through the clean setup.

---

# 1️⃣ Create a Self-Signed SSL Certificate

Run this on your server:

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /etc/nginx/ssl

sudo openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 \
-newkey rsa:2048 \
-keyout /etc/nginx/ssl/selfsigned.key \
-out /etc/nginx/ssl/selfsigned.crt
```

It will ask questions like:

```
Country Name
State
Organization
Common Name
```

For **Common Name**, use your server name or IP:

```
Common Name: your_domain_or_ip
```

Example:

```
Common Name: 10.10.24.188
```

---

# 2️⃣ Configure Nginx SSL Reverse Proxy

Edit your nginx site config:

```bash
sudo nano /etc/nginx/sites-available/app
```

Example configuration:
# ---------------------------
# HTTP → HTTPS redirect
# ---------------------------
server {
    listen 8080;  # you can use 80 if this is for wider use
    server_name your_domain_or_ip;

    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}

# ---------------------------
# Gunicorn App (local production)
# ---------------------------
server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    server_name 10.10.24.188;

    # SSL self-signed for local Gunicorn
    ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/selfsigned.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/selfsigned.key;

    # SSL Settings
    ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
    ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;
    ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;
    ssl_session_timeout 10m;

    # Security Headers
    add_header X-Frame-Options SAMEORIGIN always;
    add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff always;
    add_header X-XSS-Protection "1; mode=block" always;
    add_header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains" always;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;

        # Preserve client info
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}



# 3️⃣ Enable the Site

```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/app /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
```

Test configuration:

```bash
sudo nginx -t
```

Restart nginx:

```bash
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

---

# 4️⃣ Run Gunicorn

Example:

```bash
gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 app:app
```

or with workers:

```bash
gunicorn --workers 3 --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 app:app
```

